 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 526894,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "The average potato weighs 225 grams. A grocery chain orders 5,000 bags of potatoes. Each bag weighs 5 kg. Approximately how many potatoes did they order?",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<table class=\"unnumbered\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Prefix</td>\n<td>kilo-</td>\n<td>hecto-</td>\n<td>deca-</td>\n<td>base</td>\n<td>deci-</td>\n<td>centi-</td>\n<td>milli-</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Abbreviation</td>\n<td>k</td>\n<td>h</td>\n<td>da</td>\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\n<td>d</td>\n<td>c</td>\n<td>m</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Magnitude</td>\n<td>10<sup>3</sup></td>\n<td>10<sup>2</sup></td>\n<td>10<sup>1</sup></td>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>10<sup>−1</sup></td>\n<td>10<sup>−2</sup></td>\n<td>10<sup>−3</sup></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Step 1: Convert 225 grams to kilograms to find the weight of one potato in kilograms.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"225\\cancel{{{\\text{grams}}}}\\left( {\\frac{{1{\\text{ kilogram}}}}{{1,000{\\text{ }}\\cancel{{{\\text{grams}}}}}}} \\right) = {\\text{ 0}}{\\text{.225 kilograms}}\"></span></p>\n<p>Step 2: Use equivalences to create conversion factors. Writing the units helps you understand.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"5,000\\cancel{{{\\text{bags}}}}\\left( {\\frac{{{\\text{5 }}\\cancel{{{\\text{kilograms}}}}}}{{{\\text{1 }}\\cancel{{{\\text{bag}}}}}}} \\right)\\left( {\\frac{{1{\\text{ potato}}}}{{{\\text{0}}{\\text{.225 }}\\cancel{{{\\text{kilograms}}}}}}} \\right) = \\frac{{5,000 \\times 5}}{{0.225}}{\\text{ potatoes }} \\approx 111,111{\\text{ potatoes}}\"></span></p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "111,111 potatoes"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
